Stanislaw Lem wrote a most entertaining story titled "Golem XIV" which
examines just these issues.  It is found in the collection titled
"Imaginary Magnitude".  This book consists entirely of prefaces, forewards,
introductions, etc. to imaginary books.  Several of the stories have
somewhat extropian themes, but the piece "Golem XIV" in particular examines
the notion of an ascending series of qualitatively differing intelligences,
and the types of interactions between them.

